<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="49858" href="schedule/2014/fall/ARTH/546/49858.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2014" href="schedule/2014.xml">2014</calendarYear><term id="120148" href="schedule/2014/fall.xml">Fall 2014</term><subject id="ARTH" href="schedule/2014/fall/ARTH.xml">Art--History</subject><course id="546" href="schedule/2014/fall/ARTH/546.xml">Seminar in Contemporary Art</course></parents><sectionNumber>1  </sectionNumber><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Topic: Theories of Photography.  This course introduces students to political and cultural debates around the status of the photographic image in the 21st century. Among the topics explored: documentary, witness/cell phone photography, surveillance imagery, (embedded) photojournalism, biometrics, the relationship between photography and cinema, and the relationship between photography and political rights.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>Closed</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2014-08-25Z</startDate><endDate>2014-12-10Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>05:00 PM</start><end>07:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>T      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>15</roomNumber><buildingName>Art and Design Building</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Weissman" firstName="T">Weissman, T</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>